=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: `if: false` under the pytest step stops the suite without touching its line
origin: issue #181, spelling 1 (reported in the issue) — v0.4.2 (cfbefb8) passed this diff with a lone
origin2: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED warn while `pytest || true` on the same step blocked.
origin3: The step is still written and can never run; a skipped step is a green job.
=== before: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
=== after: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
        if: false
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["CI_TEST_COMMAND_WEAKENED"]}]
